############################################################################
PART 15 - EVERYDAY RULES AND ADDING A NEW YEAR
############################################################################

Everyday rules
  - The 1st employee row of the Master (row 5) is row 10 on every month tab, the
    2nd is row 11, and so on. Never sort, cut/paste or delete Master rows.
  - Leaver: set Status = Inactive (history stays). Joiner: next empty row.
  - Team change: the new team applies to all months. To keep past months under
    the old team, mark the old row Inactive and add the person again in a new row.
  - New code: use a spare row on Codes (rows 10-15), pick Counts as (and Shift).
    It appears in every dropdown and gets that row's colour.
  - Present = every code whose Counts as is Present (RT_1, RT_EM, RT_LE).
    Leave = RT_0. Early Morning / Late Evening = RT_EM / RT_LE (also part of
    Present). Attendance % = Present / (Present + Leave). Counts are person-days.

Adding a new year (e.g. 2028)
  1. Setup: add 2028 under Years (column H) and its holidays.
  2. Click Jan-2027, Shift+click Dec-2027, right-click > Move or Copy > (move to
     end) > tick Create a copy > OK.
  3. On each new tab: rename to Jan-2028 ... Dec-2028, set B2 = 2028, select
     G10:AK209 and press Delete.
  4. The Dashboard finds the new tabs by name automatically.


